<title>UK: SOCCER-EMERSON BACK IN MIDDLESBROUGH.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-EMERSON BACK IN MIDDLESBROUGH.</headline>
<dateline>MIDDLESBROUGH, England 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unsettled Emerson returned to Middlesbrough from Rio De Janeiro on Monday.</p>
<p>The four million pounds ($6.6 million) signing has left Middlesbrough three times in the last month, saying his wife Andrea was homesick and ill in the northeast of England. She was with him on arrival.</p>
<p>Middlesbrough manager Bryan Robson said at the weekend that he has felt &quot;let down&quot; by the Brazilian's absences.</p>
<p>Club chairman Steve Gibson has refused to let Emerson move. He believes the player should honour his four-year contract.</p>
</text>
